Z||000000||LEE498||05-09-99||10:23 PM||||Do any one know how to raise the rev limiter on v6 fiero? or do i have to get an custom chip made? Any suggestions?<br>
Z||000001||Lynx||05-10-99||01:26 AM||||My suggestion is leave the rev limiter alone, its there for a reason. I dont understand why you would want to risk VERY expensive engine parts for a little more speed. 
Z||000002||LEE498||05-10-99||08:06 AM||||Well i'm in the process of building an performance engine.. I KNOW IT THERE FOR A REASON!! FOR A STOCK MOTOR! Duuuu.. Ijust wanted to know how to raise it!!   
Z||000003||Lynx||05-10-99||11:28 AM||||Usually you cant raise them you just find a way to remove it. Im sure its controled by the computer, if it was a seperate piece it would be simple like old cars. Find out if there is anything special about the rev limiter or if its just apart of the main computer. Thats a good start.
Z||000004||LEE498||05-10-99||01:09 PM||||Thank's Lynx
Z||000005||grizco||05-17-99||06:41 PM||||I think the ADS performance chips for the 2.8 V6 remove the rev limiter.
Z||000006||LEE498||05-17-99||09:21 PM||||No it doesn't i have an ADS chip and it will still shut down at 6000 rpms.86 se v6  I think 6000 will do just fine!!! 
Z||000007||theogre||05-18-99||01:54 PM||||are you guys using a stock ignition? that could be a problem as well. The stock ignition is going to have a hard time charging the coil above a certain RPM. it varies some depending on the specific motor when exactly it will happen. The end result is the same as a rev limiter.<p>You might want to contact MSD, and/or Moroso. (Does that motor even actually have rev limiting? It seems to me only the 4 cyl does.)
